\subsection{Final Evaluation}

For each cross-validation fold, the best performance metrics—recall, precision, F1-score, and accuracy—were recorded for both the illicit and licit classes. These metrics provide a comprehensive evaluation of the model’s ability to handle both classes effectively, with particular emphasis on recall for the illicit class due to its importance in detecting anomalies.

The integration of hyperparameter optimization, ensemble learning, and self-learning pseudo-labeling proved to be effective in improving the model’s performance in distinguishing between licit and illicit activities, even in the presence of substantial class imbalance.

