\subsection{Laser}
\label{sec:laser}

An NKT Photonics picosecond laser with a PiL1-040-40FC head was used for both the PDE (in a photoelectron pulse counting mode) and the QE (in a photocathode current measurement mode) evaluation.
According to its test report, the laser produced light with a wavelength of 398.6~nm. This value is used in all of our estimates. Laser light was coupled into a single-mode fiber with a nominal core diameter of 3~$\mu$m, and then into a 600~$\mu$m diameter multi-mode fiber inside of the dark box.


