A Newport MKS CS130B-1-FH monochromator with a 150~W 66477-150XV-R1 Xenon arc lamp was used for complementary QE measurements in the same setup, to observe a possible difference between a pulsed and a continuous light sources. The monochromator grating grid setting was tuned in such a way that its average wavelength as measured by a spectrometer (see Section \ref{sec:spectrometer}) was the same as for the laser. 

