It's clear that there exists imbalance in the dataset. CT1 takes the majority among all the categories (about 61.6 \%) while CT4 only takes a very small part in the dataset (about 0.2 \%). In this paper, considering the difficulties to conduct multi-label classification under the conditions of imbalance, we ignore the CT4 category and focus on building up an end-to-end machine learning model to classify CT0, CT1, CT2 and CT3. The techniques to handle the long-tail problem will be discussed in later sections.



