Class-balanced loss is equivalent to introduce a reweighting vector relevant to the number of samples per class and a hyperparameter describing the effective number of samples. Accoding to \cite{c5}, reweighting is vertical to the use of margin term. Therefore the combination of these two will become possible to bring about more benefits in boosting the performance of our system.



