Based on the above experiments, the system parameters are determined and listed in Table \ref{sys}. The m here denotes the constant coefficient of margin item of label-distribution-aware loss and s denotes expanding factor\cite{c5}. Gamma is relevant to the significance of hard samples in the back propagation process when applying focal loss as the loss function of train\cite{c6}. And beta represents the capacity of sample space of datasets\cite{c7}. 

