Let $I= [0,1]$. We say that two functors $$F _{0}, F _{1}: \Delta^{} (X) \to
w A _{\infty}Cat ^{\mathbb{Z} _{2}} _{k}$$ are
\textbf{\emph{concordant}}  if there is a functor
$$\widetilde{F}: \Delta^{} (X \times I) \to w A _{\infty}Cat
^{\mathbb{Z} _{2}} _{k}$$ s.t.
$\widetilde{F}| _{\Delta^{} (Y \times \{0\})} = F _{0} $ and $\widetilde{F}| _{\Delta^{}
(Y \times \{1\})} = F _{1} $. 
\end{definition}

