particular construction of $\operatorname {Fuk} (M, \omega
)$ is presented in Part I. To briefly outline, as part of
some perturbation data $\mathcal{D} $, for each $L, L'  \in \obj \operatorname {Fuk} (M, \omega) 
$ we have Hamiltonian connections $\mathcal{A}  (L,
L')$ on the trivial fibration $[0,1] \times M \to
