\subsection {The main lemma and immediate consequences} \label{section:immediateconsequences}
\begin{lemma} \label{lemma:nontrivialelement} 
Suppose that $P$ is a non-trivial Hamiltonian fibration and
$\mathcal{D}$ is unexcited data for $P$ as above, then $sec$ as
above does not extend to a section of $K (P _{-})$.
Moreover, unexcited data $\mathcal{D} $ exists.
\end{lemma} 
This lemma involves all the ingredients of our theory,  its
proof that will be broken up in parts, and will follow shortly.
\begin{proof} [Proof of Theorem \ref{thm:firstquantumobstruction}]
Clearly $\qobs (P) \geq 4$, since the $3$-skeleton of $S ^{4} $ is trivial. 
By Lemma \ref{lemma:nontrivialelement} above, $K (P)$ does
not have a section over the $4$-skeleton. 
\end{proof}
