\section{Conclusions}
This paper proposed an INR-based beamforming framework for CAPA systems. Two networks, BeaINR and CoefINR, were proposed. BeaINR directly learns the beamforming function over the BS aperture, while CoefINR reduces training complexity by learning a coefficient function over the user aperture. Simulation results demonstrated that the proposed methods gain over baselines in both SE and inference time, with CoefINR offering additional training efficiency. Future work will extend this framework to multi-user
and multi-cell CAPA scenarios.

