\end{align}
where  $K$ is a nonnegative locally integrable kernel ($L^1([0,T])$, not necessarily in $L^2$), $b\leq 0$ and $c \geq 0\,$,  $Z$ is a continuous martingale with quadratic variation $U$ and $g_0$ is a {nonnegative locally integrable input curve}.


