\begin{proposition}
    Any s-preferred set $\JJ{P^{s}_i} \in P^s$ is such that $\nexists \cfx_i, \cfx_j \in \JJ{P^{s}_i} \cap \CFXs$ where $\model_i(\inn) \neq \model_j(\inn)$.
\end{proposition}
\begin{proof}
    Let us prove by contradiction, assuming that $\exists \cfx_i, \cfx_j \in \JJ{P^{s}_i} \cap \CFXs$.
    Counterfactual coherence (Theorem \ref{thm:main}) requires that $\model_i, \model_j \in \JJ{P^{s}_i}$. 
    However, by Definition \ref{def:BAF}, $\model_i(\inn) \neq \model_j(\inn)$ requires that $\model_i \in \Atts(\model_j)$ or  $\model_j \in \Atts(\model_i)$, and so we have the contradiction.
\end{proof}

