The equation of state $w = p/\rho$ evolves from $w = -1$ (vacuum-dominated) to $w = 0$ (matter-dominated) during the transition, naturally explaining the transition from an accelerated expansion phase to a decelerated matter-dominated era without requiring separate inflationary and matter components.

Near the transition, the field evolution is approximately:
