\end{equation}

The step function $\Theta(k - k_{transition})$ accounts for modes that exit the 3D phase. The physical parameters include $k_c = a_c H_c$ where $a_c, H_c$ are scale factor and Hubble parameter at transition, $k_{transition} = 2\pi/\eta_c$ where $\eta_c$ is conformal time at transition, $\alpha_{trans} \sim 0.1-1$ representing the amplitude of transition effects, and $\beta \sim 0.5-2$ characterizing the spectral dependence.

