The digital receiver operates in start-stop mode, cycling through six switching states. Sixteen frames of integrated power spectra, along with markers and fixed patterns for identifying data from parallel paths, are transmitted to a single-board computer via a 1 Gigabit Ethernet User Datagram Protocol (UDP) packets at the rate of 8 MBps for further processing. There are 96 spectra obtained from six calibration states corresponding to one calibration cycle. Figure \ref{fig:fig6_SPF} depicts the signal processing flow inside the Virtex-6 FPGA. The firmware blocks within the FPGA function at a clock speed of 125 MHz.  The effective spectral resolution after windowing is about 30.51 kHz. \linebreak Table \ref{tab7} presents the specifications of the firmware architecture, resource utilization, and the timing achieved within the Virtex-6 FPGA.


